#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "237e9db9-a621-5abe-be24-d11ec63840d5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of a Matrix Using the Properties of Diagonalization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3458a6f-9c67-5e9e-bdae-7d70f0a69fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306826} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f2d51f-b847-5d55-b18a-a42942fcc046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306827} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea77758-35fa-5d1a-93fd-3e88e2d58ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306828} {:answer/id #uuid "29d4effd-0ff3-59ae-9e45-b14b22ffc070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306829} {:answer/id #uuid "75d71b7a-85b3-515f-8ff9-f8415953f187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3458a6f-9c67-5e9e-bdae-7d70f0a69fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306826} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2003b6f-0454-5988-8299-6a6315503fa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b1eed05-d07c-590e-b279-39088f439f63" :question/math-academy-id "q-37362" :question/problem "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $N$ given that \n\n$$\nN[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), right-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $N:$\n\n$$\nN={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $N$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $N$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P:$\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$"}]}
